              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "arrogāns, arrogantis — \"arrogant, presumptuous\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Iuvenis arrogāns nēminem audit. The arrogant young man listens to no one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One ending. The present participle of arrogō — to claim for oneself. English arrogant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "arrogāns is the present participle of arrogō \"to claim for oneself\", built on ad- and rogō \"to ask\" (Lewis & Short). English arrogant comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
